  "question": {
    "text": "The set $(A \\backslash B) \\cup(B \\backslash A)$ is equal to]"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$[A \\backslash(A \\cap B)] \\cap[B \\backslash(A \\cap B)]$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$(A \\cup B) \\backslash(A \\cap B)$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$A \\backslash(A \\cap B)$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\overrightarrow{A \\cap B} \\backslash A \\cup B$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given set can be written as $(A-B) \\cup(B-A)=(A \\cup B)-(A \\cap B)$\r\n\r\n(By definition of symmetric difference) Hence, $(\\mathrm{A} \\backslash \\mathrm{B}) \\cup(\\mathrm{B} \\backslash \\mathrm{A})=(\\mathrm{A} \\cup \\mathrm{B}) \\backslash(\\mathrm{A} \\cap \\mathrm{B})$"
  }
}